% Oral Anticancer Drugs: LCD L33826 and its Policy Article A52479 (DME MACs).
% A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le (orders,
% delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills) and states when a
% claim for an oral anticancer drug (busulfan, capecitabine, cyclophosphamide,
% etoposide, melphalan, methotrexate, temozolomide, topotecan — the eight
% drugs whose indications the Policy Article lists, group by group — or the
% not otherwise classified J8999) or for an antiemetic used with one (J8498,
% J8597) is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY: the statutory criteria 1-4 of the
% Policy Article (an FDA-approved drug with the same active ingredient as a
% covered injectable drug, used for the same indications, prescribed by a
% practitioner licensed to prescribe anticancer agents), the indication read
% as a diagnosis of the drug's ICD-10 group, the drug not used for
% immunosuppression, and for the antiemetic: used with a covered oral
% anticancer drug that is likely to induce emesis, within the two hours
% before it. An oral anticancer drug the article does not list (A9270) is
% never covered: it is in scope and no rule concludes it.
%
% How the criteria are read. The article's ICD-10 table is data
% (sources/icd10/A52479_icd10_covered.csv, loaded as the table
% anticancer_icd10); its eight groups are named by drug in the article, but
% the article's text file does not carry the "Group N" paragraphs, so the
% groups are mapped to the drugs in the article's alphabetical order, which
% the indications of each group confirm (group 1 the leukemias, lymphomas
% and transplant status of busulfan; group 2 the gastrointestinal, breast and
% neuroendocrine tumors of capecitabine; group 3 cyclophosphamide; group 4
% the lung, testicular and lymphoma indications of etoposide; group 5 the
% myeloma, amyloidosis and ovarian indications of melphalan; group 6
% methotrexate; group 7 the glioma, melanoma and neuroendocrine indications
% of temozolomide; group 8 the ovarian, lung and cervical indications of
% topotecan). The drugs are identified by their HCPCS J codes (J8510 to
% J8705, the standard codes of the drugs; the article bills them by NDC and
% names only J8530, J8610, J8498, J8597, J8999 and A9270): a claim's code
% stands for its drug, and a J8999 claim states the drug it dispenses. The
% finding this policy reads (dmepos.le's judged template), and the criterion
% it stands for:
%   anticancer drug likely to induce emesis (the antiemetic's criterion 2:
%   "It is likely that administration of the covered oral anticancer drug
%   will induce emesis if the antiemetic drug is not administered").
% Not modelled: the licensing of the dispensing entity, the supply fees
% Q0511 and Q0512, the NDC crosswalk, the appeal route for a diagnosis
% outside the list.
%
% The payment conditions the policy adds (LCD L33826 "Refill requirements",
% Policy Article A52479 "Policy specific documentation requirements"): no
% more than a one-month quantity dispensed at a time, and for J8498 and
% J8597 the narrative of the claim (the drug's name, manufacturer and dosage
% strength, the oral anticancer drug used and its frequency of
% administration).

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    the drug dispensed as *an item* is *a drug*; undefined.
    *an item* is approved by the FDA; undefined.
    *an item* is prescribed by a practitioner licensed under state law to prescribe anticancer chemotherapeutic agents; undefined.
    *an item* is prescribed for immunosuppression; undefined.
    *an item* is used in conjunction with *an other item*; undefined.
    *an item* is administered *a number* hours before the oral anticancer drug; undefined.
    the claim narrative for *an item* identifies *an element*; undefined.
    % the codes and the groups
    the oral anticancer drug of code *a code* is *a drug*.
    the ICD10 group of *a drug* is *a group*.
    ICD10 code *a code* is in group *a group* of article *an article* as *a description* under table anticancer_icd10.
    % derived
    *an item* is an oral anticancer drug.
    *an item* is an oral anticancer antiemetic.
    the oral anticancer drug of *an item* is *a drug*.
    *an item* meets the oral anticancer drug criteria for *a beneficiary*.
    *an item* is used for an indication of its injectable form for *a beneficiary*.
    *an element* is a required element of the antiemetic narrative.
    the narrative requirements are met for *a claim*.
    *a claim* is within the one month dispensing limit of the anticancer policy.

% The Policy Article's ICD-10 table: eight groups, one per drug.
the table anticancer_icd10 is loaded from sources/icd10/A52479_icd10_covered.csv, with all matches:
    code | group | article | description

the knowledge base oral_anticancer includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base oral_anticancer includes:

LCD L33826 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33826".
the text of LCD L33826 is at "sources/lcd/L33826.txt".
Policy Article A52479 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52479".
the text of Policy Article A52479 is at "sources/article/A52479.txt".

% What the items are, by code.
rule anticancer_drug_codes with provenance Policy Article A52479,
        confer "Oral anticancer drugs which are not covered under the oral anticancer drug benefit (i.e., those that are not specifically listed in this policy) must be billed using code A9270":
an item is an oral anticancer drug
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["J8510", "J8520", "J8521", "J8530", "J8560", "J8600", "J8610", "J8700", "J8705", "J8999"].

rule anticancer_antiemetic_codes with provenance Policy Article A52479,
        confer "A self-administered antiemetic drug billed with code J8498 or J8597 is covered if all of the following criteria are met":
an item is an oral anticancer antiemetic
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["J8498", "J8597"].

% The eight drugs of the article, by code (the standard HCPCS codes of the
% oral drugs; the texts bill them by NDC) and by ICD-10 group (the article's
% alphabetical order, see the header).
the oral anticancer drug of code "J8510" is busulfan.
the oral anticancer drug of code "J8520" is capecitabine.
the oral anticancer drug of code "J8521" is capecitabine.
the oral anticancer drug of code "J8530" is cyclophosphamide.
the oral anticancer drug of code "J8560" is etoposide.
the oral anticancer drug of code "J8600" is melphalan.
the oral anticancer drug of code "J8610" is methotrexate.
the oral anticancer drug of code "J8700" is temozolomide.
the oral anticancer drug of code "J8705" is topotecan.

the ICD10 group of busulfan is 1.
the ICD10 group of capecitabine is 2.
the ICD10 group of cyclophosphamide is 3.
the ICD10 group of etoposide is 4.
the ICD10 group of melphalan is 5.
the ICD10 group of methotrexate is 6.
the ICD10 group of temozolomide is 7.
the ICD10 group of topotecan is 8.

% The drug of an item: its code's, or, for the not otherwise classified
% code, the drug the record says was dispensed.
rule anticancer_drug_of_code with provenance Policy Article A52479,
        confer "Suppliers must use the NDC that matches the product dispensed":
the oral anticancer drug of an item is a drug
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the oral anticancer drug of code the code is the drug.

rule anticancer_drug_of_noc with provenance Policy Article A52479,
        confer "Until a new NDC number is added to the list, suppliers must submit claims using code J8999":
the oral anticancer drug of an item is a drug
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "J8999"
    and the drug dispensed as the item is the drug.

section applicability is:

% The codes this policy decides, and their benefit: the oral anticancer drug
% benefit of Social Security Act §1861(s)(2)(Q) (Policy Article A52479).
rule anticancer_codes with provenance Policy Article A52479,
        confer "Oral anticancer drugs are covered under the oral anticancer drug benefit":
the policy for code a code is oral_anticancer
    if the code is in ["J8510", "J8520", "J8521", "J8530", "J8560", "J8600", "J8610", "J8700", "J8705", "J8999", "J8498", "J8597", "A9270"].

rule anticancer_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52479,
        confer "Oral anticancer drugs are covered under the oral anticancer drug benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is oral anticancer drug benefit
    if the policy for code the code is oral_anticancer.

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The oral anticancer drug: the statutory criteria 1-4, the indication of
% the injectable form, not for immunosuppression.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule anticancer_claim with provenance LCD L33826,
        confer "Statutory coverage criteria for oral anticancer drugs are specified in the related Policy Article. In addition, the drug must be reasonable and necessary for the individual beneficiary":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is an oral anticancer drug
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the item meets the oral anticancer drug criteria for the beneficiary.

rule anticancer_criteria with provenance Policy Article A52479,
        confer "For an oral anticancer drug to be covered, all of the following criteria (1-4) must be met":
an item meets the oral anticancer drug criteria for a beneficiary
    if the item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the item is approved by the FDA
    and the oral anticancer drug of the item is a drug
    and the item is used for an indication of its injectable form for the beneficiary
    and the item is prescribed by a practitioner licensed under state law to prescribe anticancer chemotherapeutic agents
    and it is not the case that
        the item is prescribed for immunosuppression.

% Criterion 3: the indication of the injectable form — a diagnosis of the
% drug's group of the article's list.
rule anticancer_indication with provenance Policy Article A52479,
        confer "It is used for the same anticancer chemotherapeutic indications, including unlabeled or “off label” uses, as the non-self-administrable form of the drug":
an item is used for an indication of its injectable form for a beneficiary
    if the oral anticancer drug of the item is a drug
    and the ICD10 group of the drug is a group
    and the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and ICD10 code the code is in group the group of article "A52479" as a description under table anticancer_icd10.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The antiemetic used with an oral anticancer drug.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule anticancer_antiemetic_claim with provenance Policy Article A52479,
        confer "The antiemetic drug is administered within 2 hours before the covered oral anticancer drug is administered":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is an oral anticancer antiemetic
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the item is used in conjunction with an other item
    and the other item is an oral anticancer drug
    and the other item meets the oral anticancer drug criteria for the beneficiary
    and the finding anticancer drug likely to induce emesis about the beneficiary is established
    and the item is administered a number hours before the oral anticancer drug
    and the number >= 0
    and the number <= 2.

section remedy is:

% The policy's own conditions of payment: at most a one-month quantity at a
% time, and the narrative of an antiemetic claim.
rule anticancer_documentation with provenance LCD L33826,
        confer "Regardless of utilization, a supplier must not dispense more than a one (1) month quantity at a time":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is oral_anticancer
    and the claim is within the one month dispensing limit of the anticancer policy
    and the narrative requirements are met for the claim.

rule anticancer_one_month with provenance Policy Article A52479,
        confer "The quantity of oral anticancer drugs that is dispensed should be limited to a 30-day supply":
a claim is within the one month dispensing limit of the anticancer policy
    if the claim is for a supply of a number months
    and the number <= 1.

rule anticancer_narrative with provenance Policy Article A52479,
        confer "Claims for codes J8498 or J8597 must identify the name of the drug, the manufacturer, and the dosage strength of each tablet/suppository/etc":
the narrative requirements are met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is an oral anticancer antiemetic
    and for all cases in which
            an element is a required element of the antiemetic narrative
        it is the case that
            the claim narrative for the item identifies the element.

% a claim for the anticancer drug itself has no narrative requirement — a
% device of this model
rule anticancer_narrative_not_needed:
the narrative requirements are met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and it is not the case that
        the item is an oral anticancer antiemetic.

drug name is a required element of the antiemetic narrative,
    as stated in Policy Article A52479, confer "must identify the name of the drug, the manufacturer, and the dosage strength of each tablet/suppository/etc".
manufacturer is a required element of the antiemetic narrative,
    as stated in Policy Article A52479, confer "must identify the name of the drug, the manufacturer, and the dosage strength of each tablet/suppository/etc".
dosage strength is a required element of the antiemetic narrative,
    as stated in Policy Article A52479, confer "must identify the name of the drug, the manufacturer, and the dosage strength of each tablet/suppository/etc".
oral anticancer drug used is a required element of the antiemetic narrative,
    as stated in Policy Article A52479, confer "The claim must also indicate which oral anticancer drug is being used and the prescribed frequency of administration of the anticancer drug".
frequency of administration is a required element of the antiemetic narrative,
    as stated in Policy Article A52479, confer "The claim must also indicate which oral anticancer drug is being used and the prescribed frequency of administration of the anticancer drug".
